OK QApplication is always created (even with --dist). Let me check: is the hang due to threading + Qt? Yes — QApplication has thread-safety constraints, and `MultiViewer` operations should be on the main thread.

But wait, the GUI calls happen in the post-loop, not in the parallel loop. Let me re-check:

Actually, looking at my parallel loop, the `intersect()` and `find_F()` don't touch Qt. The GUI is in the post-loop. So it should be fine.

But the program hangs. Maybe `get_conv_from_grid` is being called from multiple threads indirectly? Or maybe `CGAL::convex_hull_2` is not thread-safe?

Looking at `get_conv_from_grid`:
```cpp
std::vector<Point> get_conv_from_grid(const Point &p) {
    std::vector<Point> points = get_points_from_grid(p);
    std::vector<Point> conv;
    CGAL::convex_hull_2(points.begin(), points.end(), std::back_inserter(conv));
    return conv;
}
```

This is called ONCE per `cur` (outside the parallel loop), so it's serial. That's fine.

The hang is mysterious. Let me check if there's an infinite loop somewhere. Let me read the modified per-i loop more carefully:

